# The decoder's entry point.
#
# Protocol: stdin gives the input path and the output path (natively
# `/file/<absolute path>`), and optionally a third line: `nosmooth` selects
# plain replication of subsampled components, as `djpeg -nosmooth`; anything
# else, or no third line, selects fancy (triangle) upsampling, as default
# djpeg. stdout gets `FRAME width height ncomp kind`, then either `DECODED`,
# with the P5 or P6 image written to the output path, or, for input the
# decoder does not handle yet, `NOT_YET <reason>` (12-bit or 4-component)
# with no output file; the exit status is 0. A
# refusal is a trap `REFUSED CODE: message` on stderr with exit status 1; any
# other trap is a decoder bug. The output is opened before decoding, so a
# refusal mid-scan can leave a partial file: the harness ignores it, and the
# service deletes the request directory.

: main ( -- )
  read-line drop :> inp
  read-line drop :> outp
  read-line drop :> mode
  inp source.load markers.open :> j
  j markers.walk
  j huffman.scan-tables :> tabs
  j markers.frame-line println
  j rows.unsupported :> why
  why str.len
  [ "NOT_YET " why str.concat println ]
  [
    j tabs  mode "nosmooth" str.eq i32.eqz  rows.setup :> d
    outp d decoder.width d decoder.height d decoder.ncomp ppm.open :> h
    d [ ( bytes -- ) h swap ppm.row ] rows.decode
    h host.close drop
    "DECODED" println
  ]
  if ;
